  "note": "core/glow1..3 are the measured station-by-station fades of the core coverage and of the three glow gaussians' G amplitudes (out/analysis/arc_photometry.json). core_wide is the extra width the core gains towards mid-height. | haze and glow2b are ramps, not measured tables: both layers postdate the station-by-station cross-section fit, so reusing glow3's table for them would be an assumption dressed as a measurement. Resolving the profile error by |t| band showed exactly why it matters: at |t| 40-62 deg the concave side was +13 to +27% too bright and the convex side 9-15% too dark, i.e. the glow is less one-sided towards the tips than glow3's fade allows."
